---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Pricing & insurance — DuBose, M.D." active="pricing" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,88px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Pricing &amp; insurance</span>
          <h1>Pricing</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          What $100 covers, what it doesn&rsquo;t, and how your insurance
          fits. If anything is unclear, ask me in the free conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · The price card + access rate -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split even" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="amt">$100 <span>per month</span></div>
          <div class="per">per adult patient &middot; no per-visit charges</div>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Visits as your care needs them — video, home when clinically
            appropriate, clinic space when needed</li>
            <li>Direct messaging with me, answered in 1&ndash;2 business days</li>
            <li>Every result reviewed and explained</li>
            <li>Prescriptions managed; refills handled promptly</li>
            <li>Referrals and coordination across your other doctors</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork handled — disability, FMLA, insurance
            forms, letters, prior authorizations</li>
            <li>An unhurried annual review of everything</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:20px;color:var(--soft)">
            No enrollment fee. No contract. Cancel anytime, effective at the
            end of your billing month. Monthly by card or bank account;
            annual prepayment at the same price.
          </p>
          <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="small soft">
            Each adult enrolls individually: a couple is $200, three adult
            family members $300. I care for adults only.
          </p>
          <h3 style="margin-top:32px">If $100 a month is a real barrier</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:10px">
            I keep a limited number of reduced-rate memberships for people
            for whom the standard price would genuinely prevent care. There
            is no application form and no means test — it is a conversation,
            and I keep simple written criteria so it is fair. If cost is the
            thing stopping you, say so when we talk.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · What the fee does not cover -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Beyond my fee</span>
          <h2>What the fee does not cover — and how those get paid</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            My fee covers my work as your physician. Care delivered by
            others is billed by them, usually through your insurance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Labs</b>
          <p>Through your insurance — or, where I can arrange discounted
          direct pricing, passed to you at my cost, told to you before
          anything is drawn. Often a fraction of list price.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Imaging</b>
          <p>Through your insurance; I order what is needed and explain the
          results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medications</b>
          <p>Your pharmacy and insurance as now. I help you find fair
          prices; Texas law does not allow physicians to sell medications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialists</b>
          <p>Through your insurance; I refer carefully and stay involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Urgent care, ER, hospital</b>
          <p>Through your insurance, as today. My fee never replaces
          coverage for these.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
          This is why I recommend every member keep health coverage: the
          membership works alongside insurance, not instead of it.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · How your coverage fits -->
  <section class="section band-warm" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Your coverage</span>
          <h2>How your coverage fits</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Whatever insurance you have — or none — you can join. The price
            and the care are the same for everyone. Government programs add
            one signature.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Private insurance or none</b>
          <p>Sign up. That is all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicare</b>
          <p>One additional document — a Medicare private contract — is
          required by federal rules. Your Medicare continues to pay for labs,
          imaging, specialists, prescriptions, and hospital care exactly as
          before. My fee covers only my services.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicare Advantage</b>
          <p>Same private contract. If your plan is an HMO, we will talk
          through how your plan handles tests I order before you join.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Texas Medicaid</b>
          <p>A short private-pay acknowledgment is required by state rules.
          Your Medicaid continues to work outside our relationship; if you
          have traditional (non-plan) Medicaid, we will discuss how orders
          are covered first.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
        <p>
          The one exception: federal rules do not permit private arrangements
          with patients in certain combined Medicare and Medicaid programs
          (QMB and similar). If that is your situation, I will help you find
          good care instead.
        </p>
        <p>
          Using HSA funds: recent federal law may allow it for memberships
          like this one. Confirm with your tax advisor.
        </p>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Why $100, honestly -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Context</span>
          <h2>Why $100</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Concierge medicine typically charges $2,400 to $5,000 a year in
            membership fees — and usually still bills your insurance for
            visits. A single cash-pay office visit commonly runs $130 to
            $200. Direct primary care practices like this one average about
            $100 a month nationally.
          </p>
          <p>
            I can charge this because the practice is small by design: no
            office building, no billing department, no volume targets — a
            limited number of patients, each of whom I actually know. The
            price is not subsidized by anything. It is what unhurried primary
            care costs when the overhead is honest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · What's the catch? -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The limits</span>
          <h2>What&rsquo;s the catch?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            There are limits, and they are stated rather than hidden: I keep
            business hours and am not an emergency service. I take real time
            away each year. And when my panel is full, it is full; I would
            rather close enrollment than dilute attention. That is the whole
            catch.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a class="quiet" href="/agreement">Read the full membership agreement &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Questions about your specific situation?</h2>
        <p>
          Thirty minutes, by video, free — bring your coverage questions and
          I will answer them plainly.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
